---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Overview
description: Schema-derived reference docs and implementation guidance for the Aihio design system.
---
<section class="docs-page-intro">
  <p class="docs-page-intro__meta">Native web components · No runtime dependencies · Generated from one schema</p>

  <h1>A design system that reads the same way to people and to agents.</h1>

  <p class="docs-lede">
    Aihio emits machine-readable component contracts, semantic tokens, patterns, a linter, and an MCP server from one
    build. This site is generated from those artifacts and built with the components it documents — so if a page here
    is wrong, the package is wrong.
  </p>

  <aihio-cluster>
    <aihio-button><a href="{{ '/components/' | docsUrl(page.url) }}">Browse components</a></aihio-button>
    <aihio-button variant="outline"><a href="{{ '/ai/' | docsUrl(page.url) }}">Wire up an agent</a></aihio-button>
  </aihio-cluster>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="docs-section-heading">
    <div>
      <h2>Quick start</h2>
      <p>Three steps, no build step required. The stylesheet carries the tokens; the module registers every element.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ol class="docs-steps">
    <li class="docs-step">
      <p class="docs-step__label">Install the package</p>
      <pre class="docs-code"><code>npm install @luntta/aihio</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li class="docs-step">
      <p class="docs-step__label">Load the styles and the elements</p>
      <pre class="docs-code"><code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="node_modules/@luntta/aihio/dist/aihio.css"&gt;
&lt;script type="module" src="node_modules/@luntta/aihio/dist/aihio.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li class="docs-step">
      <p class="docs-step__label">Write markup</p>
      <pre class="docs-code"><code>&lt;aihio-button variant="outline"&gt;Click me&lt;/aihio-button&gt;</code></pre>
      <div class="docs-step__preview">
        <aihio-button variant="outline">Click me</aihio-button>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="docs-step__aside">
    In development, import <code>aihio/dev</code> instead to get schema-backed console warnings. The production bundle
    never imports that module, so none of it ships.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="docs-section-heading">
    <div>
      <h2>Where to go next</h2>
      <p>Four surfaces, one schema behind all of them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-feature-grid">
    <a class="docs-feature-card docs-feature-card--link" href="{{ '/components/' | docsUrl(page.url) }}">
      <h3>Component reference</h3>
      <p>Variants, examples, each common mistake beside its fix, the full API, and the accessibility contract.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="docs-feature-card docs-feature-card--link" href="{{ '/patterns/' | docsUrl(page.url) }}">
      <h3>Pattern library</h3>
      <p>Auth flows, settings panels, confirmations, and card grids as lint-clean markup to lift wholesale.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="docs-feature-card docs-feature-card--link" href="{{ '/foundations/color/' | docsUrl(page.url) }}">
      <h3>Foundations</h3>
      <p>Colour, type, space, and motion, drawn from the tokens, with the contrast contract the build enforces.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="docs-feature-card docs-feature-card--link" href="{{ '/ai/' | docsUrl(page.url) }}">
      <h3>AI &amp; tooling</h3>
      <p>Connect an agent through the MCP server, and the lint loop that fixes its markup in one round trip.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="docs-section-heading">
    <div>
      <h2>Featured components</h2>
      <p>Drawn live, and generated from <code>dist/schema.json</code> rather than written by hand.</p>
    </div>
